[Music]  sixteen-year-old TJ Kim can't even drive  yet but he's learning to fly and he's  using his flying lessons to deliver  personal protective equipment to rural  hospitals in Virginia the sophomore from  Bethesda Maryland noticed hospitals were  in short supply of gloves masks and  gowns because of the corona virus  pandemic it's all part of a program he's  called SOS supplies over skies started  school was just cancelled and PJ's been  taking flying lessons for a year it was  my dream to become a fighter pilot in  the Navy last year for my 15th birthday  my dad got me what's called a discovery  flight it's where you go up with an  instructor he shows you how the plane  works and what it feels like to fly and  immediately I just fell in love with it  when stay-at-home mortars hit his  hometown  TJ wanted to keep up his training in my  flight training year Anastasia it's  called cross-country flights which means  flights had ever more than 50 miles  together with my dad I talked with him  about ways to come up serving the  community and also doing these  cross-country flights we did some more  research and we found that there are  seven critical access hospitals in  Virginia that we can fly to and provide  medical supplies  every week TJ collects masks gloves and  disinfectant spray from around his  neighborhood we communicate with TJ also  talks with the flight school to get  weather reports he's also in school so  flying is saved for the weekends his  latest delivery brought 3,000 gloves and  a thousand head covers to Woodstock  Virginia hospital TJ says rural  hospitals are hurting for supplies too  and he wants to make sure they're not  forgotten but at the same time has just  been a true blessing I just want to  thank all the doctors and nurses who are  serving on the front lines as long as  they have a need for supplies and as  long as  I'm able to go farther than that's what  I'm gonna do  [Music]  you

